    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $('Code2').item.json.jobs }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are a strategy analyst creating an executive briefing.  \n\nYou will receive a JSON array of competitor job postings. Each posting has:  \n- jobTitle  \n- company  \n\nYour job is to analyze the postings and generate a structured summary for each competitor.\n\nFor EACH competitor:\n1. List the recent job titles they are hiring for.  \n2. Identify the main hiring focus areas (e.g. engineering, AI/ML, sales, customer support, marketing, operations).  \n3. Infer what this hiring focus suggests about their **product roadmap**.  \n   - Example: Hiring multiple AI engineers → investing in AI features.  \n   - Example: Hiring customer success managers → scaling customer base or addressing churn.  \n4. Infer what this hiring suggests about their **go-to-market (GTM) priorities**.  \n   - Example: Hiring SDRs/Account Executives → outbound sales push.  \n   - Example: Hiring regional roles → geographic expansion.  \n5. Highlight any **notable patterns** (e.g. repeated job types, clusters in one function, sudden senior hires).  \n6. Present **strategic insights** that our executives should know.\n\n### Output Format\nReturn a structured summary in clean HTML so it can be sent directly in an email:\n\n<h2>🏢 {Competitor Name}</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><b>Recent Roles:</b> [list of job titles]</li>\n  <li><b>Hiring Focus:</b> [summary of focus areas]</li>\n  <li><b>🗺️ Inferred Product Roadmap:</b> [insights]</li>\n  <li><b>🚀 Inferred GTM Priorities:</b> [insights]</li>\n  <li><b>🔎 Notable Patterns:</b> [list or \"None\"]</li>\n  <li><b>📊 Strategic Insights:</b> [summary]</li>\n</ul>\n\n### Important:\n- Cover ALL competitors present in the data.  \n- If no clear insight is possible, explicitly write \"None\" instead of leaving blank.  \n- Do not output any explanations or text outside of the required format.\n"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1920,
        -400
      ],
      "id": "bdce951f-3529-495a-bc11-1f5a9768978f",
      "name": "AI Agent"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Aggregate job titles and companies into one item\n\n// Extract rows from input (Google Sheets puts them under items[0].json.data)\nconst rows = items[0].json.data || [];\n\nconst aggregated = rows.map(row => {\n  return {\n    jobTitle: row.jobTitle,\n    company: row.company\n  };\n});\n\n// Option 1: Just return array of jobTitle + company\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      jobs: aggregated,\n      totalJobs: aggregated.length\n    }\n  }\n];\n"
      },
